<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that for every valid index `i` in the newly constructed list, the element at index `i` in the list is equal to the element at index `i` in the collection `c`. The `c.toArray()` method is used to convert the collection to an array for easy indexing. The condition `!c.isEmpty()` ensures that the collection is not empty, which aligns with the context of the comment.
